      "id": 1,
      "text": "Macungie began as Millerstown in 1776, founded by Peter Miller.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macungie%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1875 the borough changed its name to Macungie to avoid confusion with another Millerstown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macungie%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Macungie Historical Society preserves local heritage and runs a museum right in the town’s center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
